# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# **This file is not optional.** Without it gcloud generates one containing `#!include:.gitignore`,
# which has two problems here, in opposite directions:
#
#   1. It would still upload `reference/` — 1.4 GB of books and third-party source that is tracked
#      and therefore not gitignored. Every deploy would spend minutes shipping material the image
#      has no use for.
#   2. It honours `.gitignore`, which excludes `**/[Bb]in/*` — so `bin/cli` never arrives. That is
#      fine, because the Dockerfile builds the engine from source rather than copying a Windows
#      build, but it is worth knowing that copying it was never an option.
#
# Written as an explicit exclude list rather than an allowlist, because a missed source directory
# fails the build loudly while a missed exclude only makes it slow.

.git/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# Reference material: third-party books and source, read by people and never by the image.
reference/

# Local environments. Python dependencies come from requirements.txt inside the image.
python/
python-adk/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .NET build output. The image builds from source; a Windows build would be useless in it anyway.
**/[Bb]in/
**/[Oo]bj/

# Generated at runtime, not baked in. Projects created inside a container are ephemeral — see the
# note in the Dockerfile about what does not survive an instance.
projects/
src/adk_agent/apps/
src/adk_agent/artifact_versions/

# Secrets. The Agent Platform key reaches the container through Secret Manager and the entrypoint,
# never through an image layer.
*.env
**/appsettings.json

# Documentation and tests: neither is needed to run the service.
docs/
tests/
*.md
!src/adk_agent/README.md
